## Core Commands (Slash Commands)

Slash commands are special instructions you can use within Claude Code conversations.

### File Operations

#### `/read`
Read and analyze files in your codebase

```
/read src/main/java/App.java
```

**Use when:**
- You need to understand existing code
- You're debugging and need to see the full context
- You're making informed changes

#### `/edit`
Make targeted edits to files

```
/edit src/main/java/App.java
# Change line 10 from "foo" to "bar"
```

**Use when:**
- Making surgical changes to specific lines
- You don't want to rewrite the whole file
- You need precision edits

#### `/write`
Create or overwrite entire files

```
/write path/to/new-file.java
# Content goes here
```

**Use when:**
- Creating brand new files
- Replacing entire file contents
- Setting up new modules

---

### Project Navigation

#### `/help`
Get help with Claude Code

```
/help
```

Shows available commands and features

#### `/clear`
Clear conversation history

```
/clear
```

Resets the current session (keeps context knowledge but clears message history)

